- Which inputs, callers, or stored data does changed code trust, and which can lower-trust actor control?
- Does untrusted input reach dangerous sink (query, shell, template, path, URL fetch, deserializer, HTML, log), directly
  or after storage and read-back elsewhere?
- Does every changed endpoint, job, and bulk or export path check right permission on right object, not only
  authentication? Can request field, header, or identifier override it?
- Do errors, defaults, and missing configuration fail closed?
- Can workflow steps be skipped, replayed, or raced into state business rules forbid?
